\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Praise ye the Lord! 'Tis good to raise
\par Your hearts and voices in His praise:
\par His nature and His works invite
\par To make this duty our delight.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He formed the stars, those heavenly flames,
\par He counts their numbers, calls their names;
\par His wisdom's vast, and knows no bound,
\par A deep where all our thoughts are drowned.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Sing to the Lord! Exalt Him high,
\par Who spreads His clouds along the sky;
\par There He prepares the fruitful rain,
\par Nor lets the drops descend in vain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. He makes the grass the hills adorn,
\par And clothes the smiling fields with corn;
\par The beasts with food His hands supply,
\par And the young ravens when they cry.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. What is the creature's skill or force?
\par The sprightly man, or warlike horse?
\par The piercing wit, the active limb?
\par All are too mean delights for Him.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. But saints are lonely in His sight,
\par He views His children with delight;
\par He sees their hope, He knows their fear,
\par And looks, and loves His image there.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

